source: crates/safix/src/reporter.rs
expression: render_graphical(&refusal)
---
safix::bitwarden_server_mismatch

  × flake.safix.bitwarden.server declares https://vault.example.org and the
  │ unlocked client
  │ reports reaching https://vault.bitwarden.com. Nothing was read and nothing
  │ was written.
  │ 
  │ The refusal arrives before any side is read because a write against the
  │ wrong vault is not correctable by a later run: the secret is in somebody
  │ else's store the moment it lands, and removing it there does not unsend
  │ it.
  │ 
  │ safix never repoints the client — which server it reaches is the
  │ operator's
  │ own configuration. Either point the client at the declared server, or
  │ declare the one it reaches:
  │ 
  │     bw config server https://vault.example.org
